INSERT INTO `mod_lore_codex_entry` (`ID`, `Kind`, `Zone`, `SortOrder`, `Faction`, `RequiredState`, `Title`, `Body`, `Sources`) VALUES
(4000, 0, 40, 0, 0, 0, 'Westfall', 'Westfall was once the breadbasket of Stormwind, a broad country of golden fields and windmills running from the Elwynn border to the bluffs above the Great Sea. That plenty is gone. A gang of thieves calling itself the Defias Brotherhood has swept across the farmlands, its members marked by the red bandanas they wear. Farm after farm has been seized or burned, the mines and quarries have fallen into bandit hands, and Riverpaw gnolls prowl the hills in the Brotherhood''s pay. Who commands the Defias, and from where, is a question the People''s Militia has set out to answer. Mechanical harvest golems, turned against the very farmers they were built to serve, stalk the abandoned fields. The crown withdrew its soldiers rather than bear the cost of keeping them, and those who stayed feel abandoned. At Sentinel Hill, Gryan Stoutmantle has raised the People''s Militia from farmers and volunteers, sworn to win the land back. Along the western shore, murlocs haunt Longshore, and a dead captain keeps the lighthouse flame alight.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Westfall (history: breadbasket, Stonemasons, Stormwind Guard withdrawal, Riverpaw hired, harvest golems); quest 109 reward text (Stormwind Monarchy has abandoned our cause); quest 102 description; quest 141 description; quest 103 description; creature_text 234; quest 65 description (who heads up the cartel and where they are hiding); quest 153 description (red leather bandanas)'),
(4001, 1, 40, 1, 0, 0, 'The Jansen Stead', 'The Jansen Stead is the northernmost farm in Westfall, close to the bridge that crosses into Elwynn Forest. Like most of its neighbors it was emptied when the Defias Brotherhood took the region, and rusting harvest golems now creak through its untended rows while Defias footpads lurk along the road. Nearby sits the broken wagon of Theodore and Verna Furlbrow, who fled their own pumpkin farm to the west and got no farther than this. Their weary old horse, Blanchy, waits beside it.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Jansen_Stead (pre-Cataclysm section); DB spawns: Rusty Harvest Golem 480, Defias Footpad 481, Furlbrows 237/238 and Old Blanchy 582 near map 55-60,15-25; npc_text 50027 (Verna gossip); quest 151 description; AreaTable.dbc: area 916 is The Jansen Stead; creature.areaId 916 on Rusty Harvest Golem and Defias Footpad'),
(4002, 1, 40, 2, 0, 0, 'Furlbrow''s Pumpkin Farm', 'West of the Elwynn road lies the pumpkin farm of Theodore Furlbrow and his wife Verna. One night Verna woke to a commotion and found the fields full of thieves, and the couple fled in such haste that Theodore left behind his pocket watch, a wedding gift from Verna''s father, still tucked in the farmhouse wardrobe. Defias trappers and smugglers now camp among the pumpkins, and harvest watchers stalk fields no one is left to harvest.', 'quest 64 description; quest 184 description and request text; quest 12 description (Defias Trappers at Furlbrow''s Pumpkin Farm); DB spawns: Defias Smuggler, Defias Trapper, Harvest Watcher near map 45-50,20; gameobject 290 Furlbrow''s Wardrobe; DB: Benny Blaanco 502 areaId 109; Harvest Watcher spawns around 50-53,20-25'),
(4003, 1, 40, 3, 0, 0, 'Jangolode Mine', 'Cut into the hills of northern Westfall, the Jangolode Mine was once one of the region''s chief sources of ore for Stormwind City. The Defias Brotherhood claimed it along with so much else, and their trappers and smugglers keep watch around its mouth. They are not its only tenants. Deeper in the tunnels, kobolds have burrowed in to scratch at the veins for themselves, among them a rarely seen brute known simply as the Master Digger.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Jangolode_Mine (key mineral source for Stormwind, Defias held it); quest 12 description (Defias Trappers near the Jangolode Mine); DB spawns: Kobold Digger 1236 x7 and Master Digger 1424 at -9830..-9940, 1390..1455; Defias Smuggler nearby'),
(4004, 1, 40, 4, 0, 0, 'Saldean''s Farm', 'Saldean''s Farm sits just past a fork in the road north of Sentinel Hill, one of the very few homesteads in Westfall still worked by its owners. While neighbor after neighbor packed up and fled, Farmer Saldean declared that no band of thieves would drive him off his land, and his wife Salma keeps the kitchen busy with Westfall stew and goretusk liver pie. Their stubbornness has a price. Mechanical harvest watchers have overrun the surrounding fields, and thieves still prowl the roads around the farm.', 'creature_text 233; quest 9 description; quest 36 description (farm just beyond the fork in the road); quest 22 and 38; quest 142 reward text (thief caught stealing Saldean''s wagon); DB spawns: Saldean 233 at map 56,31; Sentinel Hill 56,47'),
(4005, 1, 40, 5, 0, 0, 'The Molsen Farm', 'The Molsen Farm lies in the open country west of Saldean''s Farm, another homestead lost when the Defias Brotherhood swept across Westfall. Its barns and fields now serve as a haunt for Defias trappers, and the People''s Militia counts it among the places those raiders are most often sighted. Harvest watchers patrol the overgrown rows, and the dreaded Foe Reaper 4000 is known to turn up here, as it does at farms all across Westfall.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Molsen_Farm (seized by the Defias, Harvest Watchers roam); quest 12 description (Defias Trapper sightings at the Molsen Farm); DB spawns: Harvest Watcher x7 and a Foe Reaper 4000 spawn point near map 45,35; DB: Foe Reaper 4000 (573) has 41 spawn points from about 33,19 to 65,69 (rotating spawn, not a patrol)'),
(4006, 1, 40, 6, 0, 0, 'Sentinel Hill', 'Sentinel Hill rises at the heart of Westfall, its stone tower the headquarters of the People''s Militia. From here Gryan Stoutmantle directs the fight against the Defias, while Captain Danuvin keeps watch, scouts such as Galiaan and Riell track the bandits'' movements, and militia protectors guard the slopes. The settlement around the tower offers an inn, a few merchants and a gryphon roost kept by Thor. Help from the crown is scarce. Quartermaster Lewis buys armor through a contact in Stormwind''s Old Town and has it flown in, for the capital seems to have all but forgotten this land.', 'quest 109 description (stone tower on Sentinel Hill); creature_text 821 (Danuvin''s report); creature_template subnames for 820, 821, 878, protectors 487-490, 869, 870, 874, 876; quests 6181, 6281 (Osric Strang note: a land Stormwind has all but forgotten), 6285; DB spawns: Innkeeper Heather 8931, Thor 523'),
(4007, 1, 40, 7, 0, 0, 'Gold Coast Quarry', 'Near the shore west of Sentinel Hill, the Gold Coast Quarry once yielded gold and minerals of real worth to the kingdom of Stormwind. Today it belongs to the Defias Brotherhood. Pillagers and looters work out of its pits, and Riverpaw gnolls dig in the quarry alongside them, a plain sign of how closely the Brotherhood and the gnoll packs now cooperate. Gryan Stoutmantle names it among the places where Defias plunderers do their worst.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Gold_Coast_Quarry (valuable mineral and gold mine, Defias owned it); quest 13 description (pillagers plundering the quarry, near the shore west of the tower); quest 102 description (gnolls working in conjunction with the thieves); DB spawns: Riverpaw Miner 1426 and Defias Pillager/Looter near map 30,45-50'),
(4008, 1, 40, 8, 0, 0, 'Alexston Farmstead', 'West of Sentinel Hill stand the ruins of the Alexston Farmstead. The boy who grew up working these fields became Baros Alexston, City Architect of Stormwind, but his family''s home has since been burned and taken over by thieves, and his father could save little of what they owned. Some keepsakes, Baros''s first compass among them, are said to lie hidden on the property still. Defias pillagers and looters now pick over the ruins.', 'quest 399 description (Baros Alexston, farm west of Sentinel Hill burned and taken by thieves); quest 389 description (Baros: VanCleef and I were members of the Stonemasons Guild); quest 373 (VanCleef''s unsent letter to Baros); quest 13 description (pillagers at the Alexston Farmstead); gameobject 1166 Alexston''s Chest at map 36,54; creature_queststarter: Baros Alexston 1646 starts 389 and 399'),
(4009, 1, 40, 9, 0, 0, 'The Dead Acre', 'In the southeast of Westfall, near the bridge into Duskwood, the Dead Acre is all that remains of a farm the Defias put to the torch. Its buildings are smoking ruins and its fields have burned black. Even so the land is not empty. Harvest reapers, larger and deadlier cousins of the harvest watchers, stalk the scorched rows, the Foe Reaper 4000 is sometimes seen among them, and Defias highwaymen pass through on the roads to the southern hills.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/The_Dead_Acre (Defias burned the farm and fields, Harvest Watchers roam smoldering fields); DB spawns: Harvest Reaper 115 x10, Foe Reaper 4000 spawn points and Defias Highwayman near map 60-65,60; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/The_Dead_Acre (southeast Westfall, close to the bridge into Duskwood)'),
(4010, 1, 40, 10, 0, 0, 'Moonbrook', 'Moonbrook was once a mining town and the heart of the southern Westfall farmlands, with its own mayor and even a schoolhouse, built after a travelling scholar named Stalvan Mistmantle stayed on to tutor the farm children. He was later forced to abandon his post. Long since emptied of its townsfolk, Moonbrook is now held by the Defias Brotherhood. Pillagers fill its streets, a Defias profiteer sells his wares to any buyer, and a Defias messenger travels the roads out to the quarry and the mine.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Westfall (Moonbrook an abandoned mining town; Deadmines beneath a barn); page_text 16-18 (Stalvan''s letters, schoolhouse, town mayor); quest 167 description (mine hidden beneath a barn in Moonbrook); creature_text 467 (entrance hidden in Moonbrook); quest 142 description (messenger roads); creature 1669 Defias Profiteer, Free Wheeling Merchant; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Moonbrook (once a mining town and focal point of the farmlands; Stalvan and the schoolhouse)'),
(4011, 1, 40, 11, 0, 0, 'The Cooper Residence', 'On the western side of Moonbrook stands the old house of the Cooper family, who made barrels for the townsfolk and even for a few buyers in Stormwind itself. No Cooper lives there now, and the house stands empty among the Defias-held streets. A dusty journal left inside is half business ledger and half private diary, in which Mr. Cooper wrote of handing the trade down to his younger brother.', 'quest 13633 description and reward text; page_text 3546 (Dusty Journal); gameobject 194340 Dusty Journal; AreaTable.dbc: area 4668 is The Cooper Residence'),
(4012, 1, 40, 12, 0, 0, 'The Dagger Hills', 'Behind Moonbrook the land rises into the Dagger Hills, the ridges of southern Westfall. As the People''s Militia pressed the raiders on the farms, the hardest of the Defias fell back here to plot their next move: highwaymen, pathstalkers and knuckledusters who prey on the southern roads. Not everyone in the hills is an outlaw. The dwarf brewer Grimbooze Thunderbrew keeps a camp among the slopes, and his Thunderbrew Lager travels as far as the inn at Lakeshire.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Dagger_Hills (ridge behind Moonbrook, Southern Westfall, pre-Cataclysm Defias types); quest 14 description; quest 116 description (Thunderbrew Lager from the Westfall hills); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Grimbooze_Thunderbrew (Dagger Hills, 44.6, 80.2); DB: Grimbooze 239 spawn at 44.6,80.3; quest 116 starter 346 is the Lakeshire barkeep'),
(4013, 1, 40, 13, 0, 0, 'The Dust Plains', 'The Dust Plains are the southernmost reach of Westfall, a dry expanse where Riverpaw gnolls keep several camps under their taskmasters and mystics. On the eastern edge stands an abandoned Alliance watchtower that the Defias have seized as a base for smuggling goods along the Redridge supply route. Its master, Klaven Mortwake, pores over his tomes and hunts for Venture Company formulas, and the shipments he receives from Duskwood come with guards that are no longer human. Agents of SI:7 keep the tower under quiet watch.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Dust_Plains (southernmost area, gnoll camps, Mortwake''s Tower on eastern edge); quest 2360 description; quest 2359 description and reward text; creature_text 7053 (Klaven Mortwake); DB spawns: Riverpaw Taskmaster, Mystic, Overseer near map 55-65,70-80; Klaven 7053 at 70,74; Agent Kearnen 7024'),
(4014, 1, 40, 14, 0, 0, 'Longshore', 'Longshore is the long western beach of Westfall, a stretch of sand on the Great Sea that well earns its name. Wrecked ships litter its sands and shallows, and murlocs swarm along the tideline. From time to time a murloc is found carrying a treasure map bearing the name of Captain Sanders, now in a watery grave, whose trail of clues begins at a rusty anchor on the beach. Near the far southern end lives Daphne Stilwell, wife of the smith Jordan Stilwell, who has been holding off Defias raiders with the gun she keeps in the house.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Longshore (big beach, murlocs, shipwrecks, Stilwell farm); quest 152 description (shipwrecks along the coast); quests 136, 138, 139, 140 and item 1357 Captain Sanders'' Treasure Map; quests 1650, 1651, 1653 (Stilwells); DB spawns: murloc types along the west coast; creature_loot_template: item 1357 drops from Westfall murlocs and Old Murk-Eye; Daphne Stilwell 6182 spawn at 41.7,89.2'),
(4015, 1, 40, 15, 0, 0, 'Westfall Lighthouse', 'At the southern end of the Westfall coast a lighthouse warns ships off the rocks of the Great Sea. Its keeper''s family is dead. Murlocs under Old Murk-Eye first frightened them away and left the light dark, and when the family came back to rekindle it, the murlocs returned and slew them. Since then the flame has been tended by the ghost of Captain Grayson, who died on these rocks on the night the lighthouse stood black. The matrons of the Stormwind orphanage tell spooky stories about him to the children.', 'quest 103 description; quest 104 description; quest 1687 description and reward text; DB spawns: Captain Grayson 392 at map 30,86, Old Murk-Eye 391 at 34,84; AreaTable.dbc: areas 115 Westfall Lighthouse and 26 Lighthouse, both children of 40'),
(4016, 2, 40, 1, 1, 0, 'Gryan Stoutmantle', 'Born in Westfall, Gryan Stoutmantle went north as a knight of the Silver Hand and fought on the battlefields of Lordaeron. He came home from those tainted lands to find the farms of his youth overrun by thieves and murderers, and the crown unwilling to defend them. Refusing to turn his back on the people who stayed, he founded the People''s Militia from former farmers and volunteers and made the tower on Sentinel Hill its headquarters. He tests every recruit against the Defias before inducting them in the name of the Light.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Gryan_Stoutmantle (born in Westfall, Knight of the Silver Hand, founded the Militia, Westfall Brigade); npc_text 50020; quest 14 reward text; quest 102 description; quest 109 reward text; quest 12109 and creature 26212 Captain Gryan Stoutmantle, Commander of the Westfall Brigade'),
(4017, 2, 40, 2, 0, 0, 'Edwin VanCleef', 'Edwin VanCleef was guildmaster of the Stonemasons, the craftsmen who rebuilt Stormwind after the orcs left it in ruins, and in his youth a peerless fighter. When the work was done, the nobles refused to pay what they owed. Some senior masons were offered posts in the government, but VanCleef turned them down out of loyalty to his guild, led a riot in the city and fled, swearing revenge. Mathias Shaw of SI:7 believes the vanished guildmaster and his embittered masons lie behind the Defias Brotherhood, and Gryan Stoutmantle, who knew the name well, is loath to believe so talented a man could turn scoundrel.', 'quest 141 description; quest 389 description (Bazil Thredd account); quest 373 reward text (peerless fighter, revenge has consumed him); quest 132 description; creature_template 639 subname Defias Kingpin; creature_text 639 (Our cause is righteous); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Edwin_VanCleef (pre-Cataclysm)'),
(4018, 2, 40, 3, 1, 0, 'Farmer Saldean and Salma', 'Farmer Saldean and his wife Salma are among the last farmers still holding their land in Westfall. Saldean has watched thieves run off every neighbor he had and swears the Saldeans will never leave, even as mechanical harvest watchers trample his crops. He still sells bread to passing travelers and dreams aloud that Westfall may prosper again. Salma meets hard times at the stove, proud of her goretusk liver pie and of the Westfall stew she cooks from her friend Verna Furlbrow''s recipe.', 'creature_text 233; npc_text 2414; quest 9 description and reward text; quests 22, 36, 38; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Farmer_Saldean (bread vendor); npc_vendor 233 (breads)'),
(4019, 2, 40, 4, 1, 0, 'Theodore and Verna Furlbrow', 'Theodore Furlbrow and his wife Verna farmed pumpkins in northern Westfall until thieves overran their fields one night and drove them out. Theodore had warned Saldean to leave while he still could, and took his own advice, but the couple made it only as far as the road by the Jansen Stead before their wagon broke down. There they wait, Theodore cursing their luck and Verna fretting over Old Blanchy, their worn-out horse. Salma Saldean expects her friend to settle happily in Stormwind, and Verna has sent her own stew recipe as a parting gift.', 'npc_text 50019, 50027; creature_text 237, 238; quests 36, 64, 151, 184; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Theodore_Furlbrow (pre-Cataclysm section only)'),
(4020, 2, 40, 5, 0, 0, 'Captain Grayson', 'The spectral captain who walks the Westfall Lighthouse died on the rocks below it, wrecked on a night when murlocs had driven off the keeper''s family and the light stood dark. Lingering on the shore after death, he later watched helplessly as Old Murk-Eye''s murlocs came back and killed the family outright. With no living keeper left, Grayson has taken the flame as his own charge, determined that no other sailor will share his fate. In the Stormwind orphanage the matrons tell of a pirate captain whose ship was stolen by rival pirates, and those who have seen his ghost say he certainly looks the part.', 'quest 103 description and reward text; quest 104 description; quest 152 description; quest 1687 description and reward text; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Captain_Grayson'),
(4021, 2, 40, 6, 0, 0, 'Old Murk-Eye', 'Old Murk-Eye is a murloc who prowls the southern beaches of Longshore near the lighthouse. It was he who led the raid that frightened off the keeper''s family and left the lighthouse dark on the night Captain Grayson''s ship struck the rocks. When the family returned and relit the flame, Murk-Eye goaded the weaker-minded murlocs of the shore into attacking a second time, and that raid left the whole family dead. Grayson''s ghost wants one of his scales as proof the menace is finally ended.', 'quest 103 description; quest 104 description and reward text; DB spawn: Old Murk-Eye 391 at map 34,84; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Captain_Grayson'),
(4022, 2, 40, 7, 1, 0, 'Grimbooze Thunderbrew', 'Grimbooze Thunderbrew is a jovial dwarf of the Thunderbrew brewing clan, once master of the family distillery in Kharanos, who has set up camp in the Dagger Hills of southern Westfall. He speaks almost entirely in rhyme, punctuated by hiccups, and will answer no question until a task, set out in verse, is done. His Thunderbrew Lager is prized enough that the barkeep in Lakeshire sends for it by the keg, and he dreams of distilling a private stash of sweet amber spirit, aged in charred oak.', 'npc_text 50034; quests 48, 49, 50, 51, 53, 117; quest 116 description; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Grimbooze_Thunderbrew; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Grimbooze_Thunderbrew (owner of the Thunderbrew Distillery in Kharanos, speaks in rhymes)'),
(4023, 3, 40, 1, 1, 0, 'The People''s Militia', 'With Stormwind''s soldiers withdrawn, Gryan Stoutmantle turned to the people themselves. Farmers who had lost their land, and adventurers willing to fight beside them, come to Sentinel Hill to swear to defend Westfall and restore its peace. Membership is earned in blood. Recruits are first sent against the Defias trappers and smugglers around the Jangolode Mine and the northern farms, then against the pillagers plundering the Gold Coast Quarry, Moonbrook and the Alexston Farmstead, and at last into the Dagger Hills, where the most hardened bandits have gone to ground. Around that core, Captain Danuvin hunts the gnolls who serve the thieves, the scouts gather the red bandanas that mark Defias members, and even the magistrate of Lakeshire has written begging for help.', 'quests 12, 13, 14 (descriptions and reward texts); quest 102; quest 153; quest 214; quests 143, 144; quest 109 reward text; creature_queststarter: 821 Danuvin starts 102, 878 Galiaan starts 153, 820 Riell starts 214, 344 Magistrate Solomon starts 143'),
(4024, 3, 40, 2, 1, 0, 'The Defias Brotherhood', 'The Defias Brotherhood has driven the good people of Westfall from their land, and the People''s Militia cannot fight what it cannot find. Gryan Stoutmantle needs two answers: who heads the gang, and where it hides. To get them he calls in a favor from Wiley, a rogue who can be found at the inn in Lakeshire, in the Redridge Mountains east of Elwynn. Wiley owes Stoutmantle a debt, and a rogue hears things that honest farmers never do. Someone must go to Lakeshire and make him talk.', 'quests 65, 132, 135, 141, 142, 155, 166 (descriptions and reward texts); creature_text 467, 550'),
(4025, 3, 40, 3, 0, 0, 'Keeper of the Flame', 'The Westfall Lighthouse has seen two tragedies. The first came on the night Old Murk-Eye''s murlocs frightened the keeper''s family away and the flame went out, so that Captain Grayson''s ship struck the rocks and he died on the shore. The second came when the family returned to relight the beacon and the murlocs attacked again, killing them while Grayson''s ghost looked on. Since then the dead captain has made himself the keeper. He seeks oil for the lamp, drained from the harvest golems that roam the farms, and wants the murlocs crowding the coast thinned so that shipwrecked sailors might reach the beaches safely. Above all he wants Old Murk-Eye slain, so that many lives may be spared even if his own cannot be.', 'quests 103, 104, 152 (descriptions and reward texts); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Captain_Grayson (Horde players could do his quests before Cataclysm)'),
(4026, 3, 40, 4, 1, 0, 'The Last Farmers', 'Not every story in Westfall is one of battle. On the northern road, Theodore and Verna Furlbrow wait beside a broken wagon, having fled their pumpkin farm in the night. Theodore mourns the pocket watch left in the farmhouse wardrobe, a wedding gift from Verna''s father. Verna worries over their tired horse, Old Blanchy, and before leaving sends her Westfall stew recipe to her friend Salma Saldean. A little way south, the Saldeans refuse to go at all. Salma cooks for anyone who lends a hand, while Farmer Saldean pays to have the harvest watchers cleared from his fields and his neighbors'' too, still hoping Westfall may one day prosper again.', 'quests 9, 22, 36, 38, 64, 151, 184 (descriptions, request and reward texts)');
INSERT INTO `mod_lore_codex_part` (`Entry`, `Part`, `MinState`, `MaxState`, `Body`, `Sources`) VALUES
(4002, 1, 0, 255, 'The thieves took more than the farm. The deed to the land, signed by Theodore and cosigned by Verna, later turned up among the Defias of Elwynn Forest. On its back a gang member had scrawled that they leaned on Furlbrow to get it, and that it might serve as a model for forging a deed of their own.', 'quest 184 description (note on the back of the deed); creature_loot_template: item 1972 Westfall Deed drops from Defias Bandit, Rogue Wizard, Dockmaster and others in Elwynn'),
(4004, 1, 0, 255, 'The thieves did not stop at the fields. One was caught red-handed trying to make off with the Saldeans'' wagon, and to save his own neck he offered the People''s Militia the one thing it wanted most: to lead them to the secret hideout of the Defias Brotherhood.', 'quest 142 reward text'),
(4008, 1, 0, 255, 'The farm''s son had an old tie to the Brotherhood''s master. As young men Baros Alexston and Edwin VanCleef were fellow Stonemasons, rebuilding Stormwind together, and when VanCleef fell in the Deadmines an unsent letter addressed to Baros was found on his body.', 'quest 373 description (letter found on VanCleef''s person); quest 389 description (VanCleef and I were members of the Stonemasons Guild)'),
(4010, 1, 0, 255, 'Moonbrook hides more than its streets show. Beneath one of its barns lies the concealed entrance to the Deadmines, a vast mine burrowing deep under the town. There, out of sight of the People''s Militia, the Defias Brotherhood keeps its true hideout.', 'quest 155 description and reward text; creature_text 467 (the entrance is hidden here in Moonbrook); quest 167 description (a vast mine hidden beneath a barn in Moonbrook)'),
(4011, 1, 13, 255, 'Far to the north, at the Argent Tournament in Icecrown, a champion calling himself the Black Knight claims to be descended from the Coopers of Westfall. Dark rumors follow him: every rider scheduled to face him in the lists has met an untimely end, and the tournament''s officials want his story looked into.', 'quest 13633 description'),
(4011, 2, 13, 255, 'The journal makes no mention of children. If Mr. Cooper ever had an heir he never wrote of one, and the trade passed to his brother instead. The Black Knight''s claimed descent looks like a sham, and the tournament''s officials, fearing something worse than dishonor, have chosen to watch him quietly rather than confront him.', 'quest 13633 reward text; page_text 3546 (Dusty Journal)'),
(4013, 1, 0, 255, 'The chest from Duskwood gave up the tower''s secret. A book inside told how the Zanzil trolls of Stranglethorn had learned to raise the dead with poison, which explained the shambling drones outside Mortwake''s tower, the strange shipments out of Duskwood and the Venture Company''s dealings with the Defias. Mortwake himself gloats that Stormwind''s fallen will rise to fight for the Brotherhood.', 'quest 2359 reward text; creature_text 7053 (Stormwind forces cut down... rise and fight alongside the Brotherhood)'),
(4014, 1, 0, 255, 'Sanders laid his trail with care. A crab scuttled out of his sand-filled footlocker by the anchor clutching the next clue, which pointed east up the bluffs to an old barrel by a ruined chimney beside the road. From there the trail ran north to an empty whiskey jug beside a lone windmill on the sea bluffs, and at last west into the sea itself, to the island where the old captain''s treasure chest waits.', 'quest 136 reward text (crab with the clue); quests 138, 139 descriptions (barrel by the chimney, jug by the windmill); quest 140 description (swim west to the island with the chest)'),
(4016, 1, 13, 255, 'War in Northrend has drawn the militia far from its own fields. Under the name of the Westfall Brigade, Stoutmantle''s men have carried their banner to the Grizzly Hills, sent to find a path into the northern territories and to secure resources for the king, and Captain Gryan Stoutmantle commands their encampment there.', 'quest 12109 description; creature 26212 Captain Gryan Stoutmantle, Commander of the Westfall Brigade'),
(4017, 1, 0, 255, 'Proof was not long in coming. The Brotherhood''s messenger rode the roads of Westfall threatening death in the name of Edwin VanCleef, and the message he carried showed beyond doubt that VanCleef gives the orders. His followers call him the Defias Kingpin, and he has drawn gnolls, kobolds and even goblins to his cause.', 'quest 142 reward text; creature_text 550 (Die in the name of Edwin Van Cleef); creature_template 639 subname Defias Kingpin; quest 132 description'),
(4017, 2, 0, 255, 'VanCleef was found at last in the Deadmines beneath Moonbrook, aboard the great ship his Brotherhood was fitting out in a hidden cove. He fell fighting, crying to the end that his cause was righteous. Gryan Stoutmantle, who took no joy in condemning any man, hailed his death as the beginning of the end for the Defias Brotherhood.', 'quest 166 description and reward text; creature_text 639 (Fools! Our cause is righteous!); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/The_Deadmines (pre-Cataclysm: VanCleef aboard the Defias ship in Ironclad Cove); DB: Deadmines spawns Goblin Shipbuilder 3947, Mr. Smite 646 (The Ship''s First Mate), Cookie 645 (The Ship''s Cook), Defias Pirate 657, gameobjects Defias Cannon and Mast Room Door'),
(4023, 1, 0, 255, 'Those who come back from the Dagger Hills have earned their place. Gryan Stoutmantle, who left the tainted lands of Lordaeron only to find his homeland in a grim state, sees in their valor proof that there is hope for Westfall yet, and with great pride he inducts each of them into the People''s Militia under the Light.', 'quest 14 reward text'),
(4024, 1, 0, 255, 'Wiley talked, though he feared it would cost him his life. The gang was up to something big, he said, working hand in hand with gnolls, kobolds and even goblins. His note held one more thing, perhaps a slip of the tongue: a mention of the Stonemasons. Only one man could say what that meant, and Stoutmantle sent the note on to Mathias Shaw, head of SI:7 in Stormwind.', 'quest 132 description and reward text; quest 135 description'),
(4024, 2, 0, 255, 'Shaw made the connection. The Stonemasons'' Guild had been run by Edwin VanCleef, the builder responsible for raising Stormwind again after the orcs razed it in the First War, and when the work was done he and his men had been bitterly unhappy with their treatment by the crown. That, Shaw judged, might explain a great deal, and he wrote a full account for Stoutmantle at once.', 'quest 135 reward text; quest 141 description'),
(4024, 3, 0, 255, 'Stoutmantle knew the name well and was shaken that so industrious a man could become such a scoundrel, but he wanted proof. It came from a Defias messenger seized on the roads between Moonbrook, the quarry and the mine, whose message showed beyond doubt that VanCleef was in charge. Then luck turned: a thief caught stealing Saldean''s wagon offered to lead the militia to the hideout in exchange for his life.', 'quest 141 reward text; quest 142 description and reward text'),
(4024, 4, 0, 255, 'The traitor kept his word, though the Brotherhood wanted his head and came after him on the way. He led the militia into Moonbrook and showed them the hidden entrance beneath a barn: the Deadmines, where VanCleef and his men were holed up. With the lair found, Stoutmantle declared VanCleef as good as theirs.', 'quest 155 description and reward text; creature_text 467'),
(4024, 5, 0, 255, 'One task remained. Stoutmantle took no joy in condemning any man to death, but for the good of Westfall he ordered VanCleef slain. Champions went down into the Deadmines and came back with the Kingpin''s head, and Stoutmantle hailed his death as the beginning of the end for the Defias Brotherhood, hoping that peace would soon grace the plains again.', 'quest 166 description and reward text'),
(4025, 1, 0, 255, 'Old Murk-Eye is dead at last. Grayson knows it cannot undo the deaths of the keeper''s family or his own, but by that slaying, he says, one life was laid to rest and perhaps many more were saved, and the Great Sea is a little safer each night the flame burns above the rocks.', 'quest 104 reward text; quest 103 reward text'),
(4026, 1, 0, 255, 'The Furlbrows'' deed found its way home. Theodore had believed it gone for good, taken by ruffians who meant to copy it for forgeries. Westfall is no longer fit for honest folk, he says, and the couple are leaving with no plans to return soon, but if better days ever come, those papers will let them reclaim their land.', 'quest 184 description, request and reward texts');
